xnu 0461: does the fetched image execute

Measured 2026-11-26: with the SMMU map cut to the 512 KiB BHI advertises, no
read faults, so the PBL performs one sequential transfer and does not load ELF
segments by offset. The image therefore lands in SRAM as a blob; whether the
code at the entry point runs is a separate question from whether the doorbell
was consumed.

The WLAON cookie and warm entry are cleared before the doorbell and written by
the firmware that starts afterwards. Reading them at +100 ms and after the 10 s
poll separates "the blob was fetched and executed" from "the blob was fetched
and never ran", which is the difference between a broken BHIe handoff and a
blob the ROM cannot enter.

